Hi,

It is a typo=E2=80=A6 Anyway, it still to be decided how to handle =
resumption in 1.3.
We still don=E2=80=99t know how resumption will be modified because of =
the PFS problem. Maybe we will simply discard it in favour of another =
mechanism if the WG considers it is good enough, for instance a =
potential 0RTT, but from last week interim meeting I think we are far =
from consensus...
I don=E2=80=99t expect this part of the draft to end up on Eric=E2=80=99s =
todo list until the WG agree upon a concrete solution.

Cheers,
B.

> On 29 Oct 2014, at 12:39, Thulasi <thulasi.goriparthi@gmail.com> =
wrote:
>=20
> In Figure 3 (Message flow for an abbreviated handshake),
> what does ClientKeyExhange message along with ClientHello signify?=20
>=20
> Thanks,
> Thulasi.
>=20
> On 28 October 2014 03:40, Internet-Drafts Administrator [via IETF] =
<[hidden email] =
<x-msg://6/user/SendEmail.jtp?type=3Dnode&node=3D436714&i=3D0>> wrote:
>=20
> A New Internet-Draft is available from the on-line Internet-Drafts =
directories.=20
>  This draft is a work item of the Transport Layer Security Working =
Group of the IETF.=20
>=20
>         Title           : The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol =
Version 1.3=20
>         Authors         : Tim Dierks=20
>                           Eric Rescorla=20
>         Filename        : draft-ietf-tls-tls13-03.txt=20
>         Pages           : 93=20
>         Date            : 2014-10-27=20
>=20
> Abstract:=20
>    This document specifies Version 1.3 of the Transport Layer Security=20=

>    (TLS) protocol.  The TLS protocol provides communications security=20=

>    over the Internet.  The protocol allows client/server applications =
to=20
>    communicate in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping,=20
>    tampering, or message forgery.=20
>=20
>=20
> The IETF datatracker status page for this draft is:=20
> https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-tls13/ =
<https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-tls13/>
>=20
> There's also a htmlized version available at:=20
> http://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-ietf-tls-tls13-03 =
<http://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-ietf-tls-tls13-03>
>=20
> A diff from the previous version is available at:=20
> http://www.ietf.org/rfcdiff?url2=3Ddraft-ietf-tls-tls13-03 =
<http://www.ietf.org/rfcdiff?url2=3Ddraft-ietf-tls-tls13-03>
>=20
>=20
> Please note that it may take a couple of minutes from the time of =
submission=20
> until the htmlized version and diff are available at tools.ietf.org =
<http://tools.ietf.org/>.=20
>=20
> Internet-Drafts are also available by anonymous FTP at:=20
> ftp://ftp.ietf.org/internet-drafts/ =
<ftp://ftp.ietf.org/internet-drafts/>=20
>=20
